#
# What was spent in a category this month, in Sutra (larder_rules.h LR1):
# closing - opening of the category's holder account, in integer minor
# units, one category per row. A holder account is never below zero, so
# both balances are 9(18): a negative balance or one past 18 digits is a
# size error, refused. The answer is s9(18): below 0 when more came back
# than went in. spent.tb says the same in Trebago.
record larder-spent
  opening: 9(18)
  closing: 9(18)
  spent: s9(18)
procedure
  compute spent = closing - opening
  answer spent
